SDL3 change: the Sound Blaster ring queues five device buffers ahead of the
card instead of four. SDL3's audio thread is cooperative and runs only while
the main thread yields, so the ring is the longest the main thread may go
without yielding: 4 x 4096 frames = 372 ms at 44100 Hz was not enough for the
Korean MI1 Ultimate Talkie at P75 (its lookout room entry runs ~460 ms); 5 give
465 ms. The ring is still allocated at a power of two for the ISR's masks
(128 KB instead of 64 KB, locked); the fill stops at five buffers, so the added
output latency is one buffer (93 ms at 44.1 kHz, 186 ms on an SB Pro at
22 kHz). The build defines DOS_SBRingChunks, which the port logs and links
against; build-dos.sh refuses an SDL3 without it.

Base: the seven earlier patches applied (~/opt/src/SDL3 branch dos-sb-ring =
dos-sb-stats 9a55c71 + this, 3ed5eb3). Apply after those (git apply skips this text):
  git -C SDL3 apply sdl3-sb-ring.patch

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index fa96a22..0555316 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -80,9 +80,20 @@ static Uint8 ReadSoundBlasterDSP(void)
 // (using the full SDL pipeline with all its allocations and mutexes), and
 // the ISR just does a memcpy (no SDL calls, no DPMI, no allocator).
 
-// Number of DMA half-buffers that fit in the ring. Must be a power of two.
-// 4 chunks is ~45 ms at 44100 Hz, enough headroom for 22 fps frame times.
-#define RING_BUFFER_CHUNKS 4
+// Number of DMA half-buffers the ring holds: what the audio thread queues
+// ahead of the card, so the longest the main thread may go without yielding
+// (4096-frame chunks at 44100 Hz: 93 ms each; 5 hold 465 ms, which a Korean
+// hi-res frame of the MI1 talkie at P75 needs). The ring itself is allocated
+// at the next power of two, which the ISR's masks need; the fill stops at
+// this many chunks, so the latency is this many, not the allocation.
+#ifndef RING_BUFFER_CHUNKS
+#define RING_BUFFER_CHUNKS 5
+#endif
+
+/* The ring's chunk count, for the program to check and log: the ScummVM DOS
+   port refuses (and fails to link against) an SDL3 without it. */
+extern const int DOS_SBRingChunks;
+const int DOS_SBRingChunks = RING_BUFFER_CHUNKS;
 
 // All of the following statics are memory-locked, making them safe to access
 // from the ISR without risking a page fault or DPMI re-entrance.
@@ -192,7 +203,7 @@ const int DOS_SBShutdownChecked = 1;
 static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
 {
     struct SDL_PrivateAudioData *hidden = device->hidden;
-    const int size = hidden->ring_size;
+    const int size = hidden->chunk_size * RING_BUFFER_CHUNKS; // the fill limit, not the allocation
 
     // Slow mixing can keep the ring below capacity indefinitely. Yield even
     // when there is room so the cooperative main thread can process events.
